{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FaddeevUniquenessBoundedCapstone","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.FaddeevUniquenessBoundedCapstone","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.BoundedMeromorphicLiouville","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FaddeevPhiUniquenessAssembly"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FaddeevUniquenessBoundedCapstone.faddeevPhi_proportional_of_bounded_ratio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FaddeevUniquenessBoundedCapstone.faddeevPhi_proportional_of_bounded_ratio","kind":"theorem","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FaddeevUniquenessBoundedCapstone.lean#L36-L62","doc":"**Boundedness-route capstone: bounded ratio ⇒ proportional.** Two `FaddeevPhi`\nsolutions at `b` (nondegenerate lattice `(b²).im ≠ 0`) whose normal-form ratio\n`toMeromorphicNFOn (Φ₁/Φ₂) univ` is **bounded** (the state-integral endowment) are\nproportional on `Φ₂`'s nonvanishing locus — provided the normal-form representative\nagrees with `Φ₁/Φ₂` there (`hr_ratio`) and the two `FaddeevPhi` periodicity loci are\ndense off `Φ₂`'s zeros (`hmem₀/hmem₁`). The `hr_entire` input is discharged\ninternally by `entire_toMeromorphicNFOn_of_bounded`; the remaining hypotheses are the\nsame honest, non-axiomatised residual analytic inputs as the divisor-route capstone,\nwith the same-divisor premise replaced by a strip growth bound. ","signatureChunk":0}]}